@@ -6,3 +6,16 @@ package holds the order book, in TypeScript; the shop's website and its staff to
 `src/index.ts`.
 
 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Discount codes
+
+A customer can give an order one discount code with `orders.applyCode(orderNumber, code)`. A second code replaces
+the first. The code takes its discount off the order's items; shipping is not discounted, and whether the order ships
+free is still decided on its items before the discount.
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € off the items, and only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+
+An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with a message saying why, and the order keeps the code
+it had before. An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items
+minus discount plus shipping.
